'''Ponda Baba''' was a [[Gender|male]] [[Aqualish]] thug who rescued [[Doctor|Dr.]] [[Cornelius Evazan]] from a [[bounty hunter]]. The two formed a partnership and began to [[Smuggler|smuggle]] [[spice]] for the [[crime lord]] [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure|Jabba]] the [[Hutt]], resulting in him becoming a wanted man. Shortly before the [[Battle of Yavin]], he was a patron in [[Chalmun's Spaceport Cantina]] on the [[planet]] [[Tatooine]], where he instigated an argument with [[Luke Skywalker]] while bored and drunk. Evazan claimed that Baba did not like Skywalker and began to threaten the youth, leading to a brief confrontation with [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]], who, after failing to calm tensions with the [[pirate]]s, used [[Obi-Wan Kenobi's third lightsaber|his lightsaber]] to sever Baba's right [[Limb|arm]]. Kenobi, who was secretly one of the last remaining [[Jedi Master]]s of the nearly extinct [[Jedi Order]], wounded Evazan with a slash across the torso when the pair drew their [[blaster pistol]]s on the old man. Evazan later tried to reattach Baba's arm using his medical training, but ended up nearly [[Death|killing]] the Aqualish in the process when the procedure failed.

==Biography==
===Early career===
{{Quote|You just watch yourself. We're wanted men.|Cornelius Evazan|<ref name="Episode IV" />}}
[[Homeworld|Originally]] from the [[planet]] [[Ando]], Ponda Baba was a burly [[Aqualish]] thug who rescued [[Cornelius Evazan]], a former [[doctor]] who was infamous for the cruelty he inflicted upon his patients, from a [[Unidentified bounty hunter (Cornelius Evazan)|bounty hunter]]. The two formed a partnership<ref name="Ultimate SW" /> after Evazan hired him for protection.<ref name="HC 4">{{HelmetCollectionCite|4|Databank A-Z}}</ref> They began to [[Smuggler|smuggle]] [[spice]] for [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure|Jabba]] the [[Hutt]]. The [[pirate]]s<ref name="Ultimate SW" /> were successful at their trade<ref name="Card Trader">{{SWCT|set=Base Series 1|cardname=Ponda Baba - Cantina Patron}}</ref> and became infamous.<ref name="Aphra 26">[[Doctor Aphra (2016) 26|''Doctor Aphra'' (2016) 26]]</ref> However, they became wanted men in several [[star system]]s, although they were mainly wanted because of Evazan's failed and sadistic surgeries.<ref name="HC 4" /> Their working relationship wasn't always pleasant, however, and Baba even briefly considered turning Evazan in to collect the [[bounty]] on his head before realizing that their ongoing partnership was more profitable.<ref name="Card Trader" /> Still, the two considered each other friends<ref name="Doctor Cornelius Evazan">{{Databank|doctor-cornelius-evazan|Doctor Cornelius Evazan}}</ref><ref name="Ponda Baba" /> despite their differences.<ref name="Card Trader" />

===Prison Escape===
Sometime between around [[8 BBY]] and [[2 BBY]], Evazan and Baba became incarcerated on the [[prison]] planet of [[Gulhadar III|Gulhadar]], at a facility of the [[Benelex Marshal Service]], and were condemned to death. During their imprisonment they witnessed the [[Wookiee]] [[Chewbacca]] being transferred over as a fellow prisoner. Evazan pointed out the fact to Baba, referring to Chewbacca as "fresh meat". The guard accompanying Chewbacca ordered Evazan to keep moving. Eventually, the duo were taken to the execution chamber, but the [[dioxis]] [[gas]] meant to kill them was redirected by fellow prisoner [[Phaedra]] and [[Maz Kanata]] broke into the room to rescue them. The duo were used by Phaedra and Kanata for their escape plan and successfully ran away from the prison.

===Wandering on Jedha===
[[File:PondaEvazan.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Cornelius Evazan and Ponda Baba on Jedha.]]
The pair eventually adopted the aliases "Roofoo" and "Sawkee," and when visiting [[Milvayne]], they committed a series of crimes including kidnapping, forced servitude, and surgical alteration. The [[Milvayne Authority]] [[officer]] [[Tam Posla]] looked into their case and despite being taken off it by [[Tam Posla's superior officer|his superior officer]] he managed to track them to [[Jedha]], where the two began creating the [[decraniated]].<ref name="The Ultimate Visual Guide">''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]''</ref> Posla traveled to Jedha to look for them and found their decraniated prototype [[Caysin Bog]], whom he fell in love with.<ref name="Aphra 18">[[Doctor Aphra (2016) 18|''Doctor Aphra'' (2016) 18]]</ref> While on their way off-world,<ref name="Baba Escape">{{Twitter|GaryWhitta|status/811351220648431616|[[Gary Whitta]]|quote=They were on their way off-world. Lucky escape, not quite so lucky later in the week.|archivefile=File:Evazan_escape.png}}</ref> Baba and Evazan bumped into the rebel operatives [[Jyn Erso]] and [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]]. Evazan told them to watch themselves and Andor said they would be careful. The two parties then continued their routes.<ref name="RougeOne">''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref> Baba and Evazan departed<ref name="Baba Escape" /> from the city prior to its [[Destruction of Jedha City|destruction]] by the Death Star<ref name="RougeOne" /> and traveled to the planet [[Tatooine]].<ref name="Episode IV" />

===Encountering Skywalker===
[[File:Bar_fight.jpg|thumb|right|220x220px|Baba and Evazan are confronted by Obi-Wan Kenobi]]
Prior to the [[Battle of Yavin]], Baba and Evazan were patrons at [[Chalmun's Spaceport Cantina]] on [[Tatooine]].<ref name="Episode IV" /> Bored and looking for excitement,<ref name="Ponda Baba" /> a drunk Baba<ref name="Ultimate SW" /> decided to pick a fight with [[Luke Skywalker]],<ref name="Ponda Baba" /> a young [[farm]]boy. Evazan quickly escalated the argument, even beginning to threaten the boy before attracting the attention of [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]], Skywalker's guardian.<ref name="Episode IV" /> The hermit attempted to ease tensions<ref name="Mos Eisley Cantina">{{Databank|mos-eisley-cantina|Mos Eisley Cantina}}</ref> by offering to purchase the pair drinks,<ref name="Episode IV" /> but Evazan and Baba both failed to realize Kenobi was asking them to stop.<ref name="HC 4" /> Thus, Evazan refused to back down and tossed Skywalker out of his way, and, along with Baba, drew his [[blaster pistol]] on the old man, despite the protest of [[Wuher]], the [[cantina]]'s [[bartender]]. Before the pirates were even able to discharge their weapons, however, Kenobi had already ignited [[Obi-Wan Kenobi's third lightsaber|his]] [[lightsaber]],<ref name="Episode IV" /> swiftly [[Dismemberment|removing]] Baba's right [[Limb|arm]] and wounding Evazan with a slash across his torso, decisively ending the argument.<ref name="Ponda Baba" />

Following the altercation, those present in the cantina briefly turned to see what had transpired before returning to their business. However, a departing patron, [[Garouf Lafoe]],<ref name="CL">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> decided to inform a [[squad]] of Mos Eisley's [[Desert stormtrooper|sandtroopers]] of the attack.<ref name="Mos Eisley Cantina" /> After the [[trooper]]s had entered the establishment and reached the counter, Wuher indicated to them where Kenobi and Skywalker had taken a seat, though the pair found another exit before they could be apprehended.<ref name="Episode IV" /> Evazan tried to reattach Baba's arm using his medical training, but ended up nearly [[Death|killing]] the Aqualish in the process when the procedure failed.<ref name="Updated and Expanded">''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia: Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> Ponda would later regret bullying that "blond human teenager."<ref name="CL" />

Skywalker later recalled his encounter with Baba while he was training with [[Skywalker lightsaber|his own]] lightsaber in the [[Temple of Eedit]] on [[Devaron]].<ref name="The Weapon of a Jedi">''[[The Weapon of a Jedi: A Luke Skywalker Adventure]]''</ref>

===Later adventures===
[[File:PondaGetsNewArm-2016DoctorAphra28.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Ponda Baba gets a new cybernetic arm.]]Baba's severed arm eventually came into the hands of Posla when he continued investigating the pair. Posla put the arm in a jar and stored it on [[Posla's ship|his ship]].<ref name="Aphra 22">[[Doctor Aphra (2016) 22|''Doctor Aphra'' (2016) 22]]</ref> Following Posla's death, Evazan stole the ship and rendezvoused with Baba in deep space. As he boarded Baba's ship, Evazan took Baba's arm with him to return to his companion.<ref name="Aphra 25">[[Doctor Aphra (2016) 25|''Doctor Aphra'' (2016) 25]]</ref> As Evazan worked on finishing a [[Cybernetics|cybernetic]] arm for Baba, they watched the [[chase on Milvayne]] unfold via a broadcast from [[assassin droid]] [[0-0-0]]'s [[photoreceptor]]s<ref name="Aphra 26" /> until they were captured by [[hunter]]s [[Nokk]] and [[Winloss]].<ref name="Aphra 31">[[Doctor Aphra (2016) 31|''Doctor Aphra'' (2016) 31]]</ref> Additionally, the new arm was very poorly attached, leading to a permanent falling out between Evezan and Baba.<ref name="HC 4" />

==Personality and traits==
[[File:PondaBaba-Masterwork2018.png|thumb|right|200px|Ponda Baba was an ill-tempered bully.]]
Fearsome<ref name="The Original Trilogy Stories">''[[The Original Trilogy Stories]]''</ref> and strong, Ponda Baba was an alcoholic<ref name="HC 4" /> and ill-tempered thug<ref name="Absolutely Everything You Need to Know">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]''</ref> who enjoyed bullying<ref name="Ponda Baba" /> those whom he considered to be an easy target.<ref name="Doctor Cornelius Evazan" />

Baba was a burly male Aqualish who stood 1.85 [[meter]]s tall.<ref name="Ponda Baba" /> He had [[Color|gray]] skin, black [[eye]]s, black [[hair]] on the lower part of his face, and a pair of pink tusks.<ref name="Episode IV" />

==Equipment==
{{Quote|No blasters! No blasters!|Wuher, as Ponda Baba draws his blaster pistol|<ref name="Episode IV" />}}
Ponda Baba wore an orange jacket, a brown pair of pants, a black pair of [[boot]]s, and a black belt with a gold buckle which had a holster attached to its left side to carry his [[SE-14C blaster pistol]] and a modified [[DL-21 blaster pistol]].<ref name="Episode IV" /> Evazan gave Ponda a new [[Cybernetics|cybernetic]] arm,<ref name="Doctor Aphra 28" /> which replaced the arm he lost to Kenobi,<ref name="Episode IV" /> with a [[flamethrower]] installed into it.<ref name="Doctor Aphra 28" />

==Behind the scenes==
Ponda Baba first appeared in the [[1977]] film [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']], the first installment of the ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[original trilogy]].<ref name="Episode IV" /> The original [[1976]] [[Star Wars: A New Hope (novelization)|novelization]] of ''[[Star Wars]]'', ghostwritten by [[Alan Dean Foster]], described the character, then nameless, as a "multi-eyed alien". This story's version of events,<ref name="Novelization">[[Star Wars: A New Hope (novelization)|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'' novelization]]</ref> which closely matches the film's revised fourth draft,<ref name="Revised Fourth Draft">{{WebCite|url=http://www.imsdb.com/scripts/Star-Wars-A-New-Hope.html|text=Star Wars: A New Hope Script at IMSDb|work=[http://www.imsdb.com The Internet Movie Script Database]|archivedate=20170913065016}}</ref> describes Obi-Wan Kenobi as cutting off not Baba's arm, rather Evazan's.<ref name="Novelization" /> The Evazan character dates back as early as [[The Star Wars rough draft|''The Star Wars: Rough Draft'']] from [[May]] [[1974]].<ref name="The Making of Star Wars">''[[The Making of Star Wars: The Definitive Story Behind the Original Film]]''</ref>

When filming the Ponda and Evazan's confrontation with Luke and Ben Kenobi, Ponda's [[blood]] was made from raspberry [[yogurt]] and red tempera paint. This was seen when Kenobi cut off his arm.<ref name="Much to Learn: The ALiens of Star Wars: A New Hope">{{SW|url=news/much-to-learn-you-still-have-9-things-you-might-not-know-about-the-aliens-of-star-wars-a-new-hope|text=''Star Wars'' at 40 &#124; Much to Learn You Still Have: 9 Things You Might Not Know About the Aliens of ''Star Wars: A New Hope''}}</ref>

A walrus named [[Petulia|Petula]] was used by [[Ben Burtt]] to supply Ponda Baba's vocalizations, although [[Tim Veekhoven]] and [[Mark Newbold]], the authors of the Star Wars Blog entry "Drawing from the Present: Familiar Creatures in a Galaxy Far, Far Away", were unable confirm whether the walrus was Petulia or not.<ref name="Drawing from the Present">{{SW|url=news/drawing-from-the-present-familiar-creatures-in-a-galaxy-far-far-away|text=Drawing from the Present: Familiar Creatures in a Galaxy Far, Far Away|int=Back from the Drawing Board|nolive=1}}</ref> Baba also appears alongside Evazan in the [[2016]] [[Star Wars Anthology Series|''Anthology Series'']] film ''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]'' and was portrayed by an uncredited performer.<ref name="RougeOne" /> ''Rogue One'' writer [[Gary Whitta]] disagreed with Baba and Evazan's inclusion in the film, opining that he "thought having Evazan and Walrus Man was a little too much. You have to reign in that instinct to go back and put things in just because you loved them when you were a kid".<ref name="Entertainment Weekly">{{WebCite|url=http://ew.com/movies/2017/03/24/rogue-one-revisions-tie-fighter-scene-deleted-planet-killed-cameos|text=''Rogue One'' revisions: The TIE fighter scene, a deleted planet, and killed cameos|author=Anthony Breznican|date=2017-03-24|quote="I thought having Evazan and Walrus Man was a little too much," Whitta says. "You have to reign in that instinct to go back and put things in just because you loved them when you were a kid."|archivedate=20171203190336}}</ref>

